{"author":{"id":"3f8bad4585cb0f07c6570d9e31f06264af3b0abf48efbc5a44f56df5e7a9cd45"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789410720,"nonce":"WpgrsiGYH7Z+OesFJG9lAiT4/kY=","title":"Interop tests crash under GC stress since wren_lift's VM/Shared split","message":"With wren_lift at 249c239 (runtime: split VM into the shared program and a thread's view), `ASH_GC_STRESS=1` makes haxe_imports abort (misaligned pointer dereference at 0x77fffffff9, a NaN-boxed value read as a pointer) or hang, and imports and project crash; `WLIFT_GC_STRESS=1` makes haxe_imports SIGSEGV. Verified on the tree before the cells (5a149ae) as well as after, so it is not the cells. The same runs passed earlier in the day against the previous wren_lift.\n\nThe one lldb trace so far: a Wren cycle's Gray::claim on a child pointer of 0x100000008 (the executable's image base + 8), from for_each_child in collect_with_ranges, called from run_fiber_loop's collect_garbage. So some Wren object, or something walked as one, holds a Value whose payload is the image base. Candidates: a VM field that moved into Shared and is read through the thread's view by the adapter (vm_of, enter_vm, record_for(vm.object_class)), or a root the split no longer reaches.\n\nThe adapter's build fixes for the split were only the borrow of engine and interner (vm.request_tier_up(id)) and explicit references over the raw VM pointers in enter_vm. Nothing else changed on the caribou side.","files":null}]}